3://! infinite-loops traps cleanly via the per-call fuel budget.
5://! ## The emscripten import problem
7://! Emscripten-built modules import a pile of `env::*` and
10://! etc. We stub them all to traps. If a candidate actually CALLS one
11://! (say, `printf`), it traps, we catch it, record the failure. The
14://! Exception: `emscripten_notify_memory_growth` gets a real no-op stub
15://! since memory growth is allowed (ALLOW_MEMORY_GROWTH=1).
17://! ## Memory layout
20://! into wasm linear memory. We hold a `Memory` handle and read through
21://! it. Memory growth invalidates host-side slices — we don't cache
